    "enum ledger.era.rules.PoolDefect",
    "given ledger.era.rules.PoolDefect.given_CanEqual_PoolDefect_PoolDefect",
    "object ledger.era.rules.PoolDefect"
   ],
   "reason": "why Dijkstra's POOL reaches no verdict on a registration's voting key (PoolDefect, with its equality with itself): the BLS12-381 library fails, or a key or proof is not a point the decoder admits, while it checks the proof of possession; the reference's verifier (verifyPossessionProofDSIGN) gives valid or not and has no counterpart of it. A decoded certificate cannot reach it through its point encoding, as the decoder refuses a point it would not admit; an exception of the native verifier can. A raise of POOL's own, not a verdict, and not a case of the node's flat LedgerFailure"
  }
